  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Southern Africa Advocacy Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">q	To develop and maintain a regional analysis of contemporary developments in Southern Africa;

q	To promote awareness and greater inter-regional understanding of Southern Africa issues;

q	To strengthen North-South partner/civil society/NGO links and activities;

q	To ensure policy is directed at understanding and responding to the major problems affecting the region;

q	To highlight the need for awareness of the abuses of human rights faced by the poor, rural people women and farm workers;

q	To highlight/mainstream issues facing people living with HIV/AIDS and the need to integrate HIV/AIDS work into development, human rights and conflict-related work.</narrative>
  </description>
